ds four of a kind), it\'s just a triplet. So it can be beaten by any higher triplet or combo of same type.\n\nBest move: Use **triple_with_pair: ♥7 ♣7 ♦7 ♥2 ♣2** — this is very hard to beat because the attached pair is 2s, the highest possible pair (only jokers are higher, and they can\'t form a pair combo). No peasant can legally beat this with a higher triple+pair unless they have triple 2s (impossible, only two 2s left unknown: we hold both) or triple A/K, etc., plus a pair of 2s — which we already hold.\n\nThus, this move is almost certainly unbeatable. It dumps 5 cards, including high-value ones, and very likely wins the trick.\n\nEven better: it removes our own pair of 2s, which would otherwise be hard to play safely later.\n\nAlternative: Save 2s? But if we don’t play them now, we may struggle to pair them later. Better to leverage them now in a powerful play.\n\nRocket should still be saved.\n\nTherefore, **triple_with_pair: ♥7 ♣7 ♦7 ♥2 ♣2** is optimal.\n\nReason: This move combines a strong triplet with the highest possible attached pair (twos), making it extremely difficult for either peasant to beat without a bomb. It maximizes pressure early, advances hand reduction, and efficiently uses high cards that are hard to play individually. Since we\'re the landlord, controlling tempo and forcing opponents to waste bombs is key. This play likely wins the trick outright, allowing us to lead again soon.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥7", "♣7", "♦7", "♥2", "♣2"]}'}
